WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.540
From actors standing up for writers, to getting
canceled by a superhero, filming "The Addams

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.935
Family" was a wild ride for everyone involved.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:14.940
When it comes to Gomez Addams, there are two
names who immediately come to mind: John Astin

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.390
and Raul Julia.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:21.869
Both actors helped to shape the beloved character
with a snappy dress style, a delightful mustache,

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:24.529
and total devotion to his wife and family.

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:29.380
Considering the Addams family members never
had first names before the television series

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.284
aired, the classic show all but shaped who
they were and how they would behave going forward.

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:38.399
However, it could have been very different
had Astin been cast for the original role

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:40.000
he was earmarked for.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.059
Speaking to The A.V.

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:45.610
Club, the actor explained how he wasn't required
to audition because of his status at the time.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.020
It also helped that he was familiar with The
Addams Family.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.540
He had collected Charles Addams' cartoons
when he was in college, so he was particularly

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.250
excited to be a part of the show.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:59.530
The role he was initially pitched was that
of Lurch — which Astin admitted seemed daunting.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.770
This plan changed, though, after producer
and show creator David Levy contacted Astin

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.387
with another suggestion.

00:01:05.387 --> 00:01:07.777
Astin told The A.V. Club:

00:01:24.023 --> 00:01:28.610
Naming a child Wednesday isn't the most outrageous
parental act ever committed.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:34.040
However, the case of Wednesday Addams is intriguing,
because it now seems like a fitting name for

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.083
her personality and appearance.

00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:38.012
"It's me Wednesday."

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:42.600
Still, one has to wonder who came up with
the idea to name her after a weekday in the

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.780
first place.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:47.540
According to a letter sent to The New Yorker,
Joan Blake claimed credit for the name after

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.540
a chance encounter with Charles Addams at
a mutual friend's party in the '60s.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.690
Blake wrote in the letter:

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.290
According to the book The Addams Family: An
Evilution, Blake's story does check out, as

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:14.540
Addams mentioned it was a friend who suggested
Wednesday after reciting the line from the

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.811
nursery rhyme "Monday's Child."

00:02:17.164 --> 00:02:20.519
There are many creators who despise adaptations
of their work.

00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:24.360
But according to The Addams Family producer
David Levy, Charles Addams was nothing but

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.879
supportive of the classic television series.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:29.620
Writing for The Los Angeles Times, Levy stated
the following:

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.580
However, Levy doesn't believe Addams would
have looked at the live-action films quite

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.350
as fondly, believing they missed the mark
of what The Addams Family was really about.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:56.720
Of course this is simply Levy's thoughts on
the matter, as Addams passed away three years

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:59.200
before the 1991 film was released.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.330
Perhaps if Addams had still been alive, he
might have had some input for the final product.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.370
Cousin Itt is arguably one of the most beloved
characters of The Addams Family.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:14.132
However, Itt didn't make his debut in Charles
Addams' cartoons, but rather the classic television series.

00:03:14.132 --> 00:03:18.849
As per The Los Angeles Times, actor Felix
Silla, who played Cousin Itt, said,

00:03:21.513 --> 00:03:25.930
Silla's sole purpose was to walk around in
costume for the scenes that required him,

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:29.737
while the lines for the character would be
dubbed in later on in the post-production process.

00:03:29.737 --> 00:03:34.720
There was one problem: Silla's costume was
made from real hair, which made it extremely

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.099
heavy and dangerous since everyone on set
liked to smoke.

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:43.939
Fearful that he might be set on fire one day,
the producers changed his costume to a much

00:03:43.939 --> 00:03:47.492
safer option, which featured synthetic, fireproof
hair.

00:03:47.784 --> 00:03:52.430
The Addams house has become a critical part
of any version of the spooky family.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:56.840
In various interpretations, it has taken the
shape of a mysterious haunted mansion, and

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.180
the classic television series employed a similar
approach as well.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.439
While most of the action took place inside
the home, which was shot in a studio set,

00:04:04.439 --> 00:04:09.823
the outside of the house was featured in the
show's intro, publicity photos, and the first episode.

00:04:09.823 --> 00:04:14.099
It would have been possible to utilize a model
house for the footage, but there was an actual

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:18.799
Addams house in Los Angeles, California — well,
for a short while at least.

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:23.210
According to 21 Chester Place, a website that
covers the history of this famous property,

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.300
the production company used the house for
stock footage.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.540
Since the company didn't own the property,
it employed an effects studio to add the necessary

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.680
details to the footage and photographs.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:37.857
Unfortunately, the fabled Addams house no
longer exists, as it was demolished in 1967.

00:04:38.413 --> 00:04:43.280
Lurch might look all doom and gloom, as if
someone stole his secret stash of chocolate

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.640
cookies, but there's a lot more to the Addams'
staggering butler than meets the eye.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:52.100
The role of Lurch is a part that features
a lot of nuance and subtlety, something not

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.970
many actors can pull off.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:58.330
Ted Cassidy not only delivered a fantastic
performance as Lurch in The Addams Family

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.820
TV series, but he also became the measuring
stick for the character that all other actors

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.380
will be judged by.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:08.700
Surprisingly, Lurch was the first television
role where viewers got to experience both

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:13.910
Cassidy's voice and face, as he had only done
voiceover work before.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:19.639
Standing at 6 foot 9, Cassidy had a successful
semi-pro basketball career, especially in

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:20.639
the college leagues.

00:05:20.639 --> 00:05:24.410
However, the entertainment bug bit when he
secured a gig as a radio DJ.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:28.040
Then, at the age of 30, he decided to give
acting a try.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:32.830
Fortunately, due to his towering frame and
distinctive voice, he was deemed the perfect

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.577
person to bring Lurch to life.

00:05:38.391 --> 00:05:39.867
"You rang, sir?"

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.551
"You're fired."

00:05:41.598 --> 00:05:46.751
Taking one look at the patriarch in Charles
Addams' cartoons and John Astin's Gomez, it's

00:05:46.751 --> 00:05:49.400
clear there are differences in their appearances.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.139
As Astin explained to The A.V.

00:05:51.139 --> 00:05:54.651
Club, the producers allowed him the space
to shape the character for the show and to

00:05:54.651 --> 00:05:56.139
tinker with the source material.

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:00.069
However, in a separate interview with the
Television Academy Foundation, he explained

00:06:00.069 --> 00:06:04.250
how he received pushback from the network,
as it wanted Astin to shave the sides of his

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.060
head to look more like the character from
the cartoons.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:12.039
Fortunately for Astin, producer and show creator
David Levy backed his ideas and ultimately

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:14.570
allowed the actor to choose the path for Gomez.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:16.238
Astin told The A.V. Club:

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.150
Astin believed this tweak to his character's
appearance further fueled the natural chemistry

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.449
between Gomez and Morticia on the show.

00:06:31.449 --> 00:06:36.039
Considering how they are still seen as a guiding
light for couples around the world, it appears

00:06:36.039 --> 00:06:38.699
as if Astin's decision was right on the money.

00:06:39.227 --> 00:06:45.319
While John Astin's Gomez, Carolyn Jones' Morticia,
and Jackie Coogan's Fester may have stolen

00:06:45.319 --> 00:06:50.550
all the limelight when The Addams Family television
series was released, the children also inspired

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:51.550
a generation.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:56.900
Lisa Loring's Wednesday became a future goth
icon, while Ken Weatherwax's Pugsley became

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:00.050
the living embodiment of the macabre nature
of the show.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:04.390
For Weatherwax, though, the role became more
of an albatross than a kick-starter for a

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.639
successful career.

00:07:05.639 --> 00:07:10.190
Speaking to Bill O'Reilly, Weatherwax revealed
how he struggled to find acting gigs after

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.308
The Addams Family, since most producers only
saw him as Pugsley.

00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:20.238
"I went out and, um, interviewed for several
roles but I was typecasted Pugsley."

00:07:20.238 --> 00:07:26.350
The role also took a toll on his personal
life, as he experienced bullying from his classmates.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.490
Weatherwax told O'Reilly:

00:07:35.528 --> 00:07:39.870
Most five-year-old children are still busy
learning to read and write, not even giving

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.390
a second thought to what they want to be when
they grow up.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:46.340
Lisa Loring admitted to The Sydney Morning
Herald the same was applicable to her, as

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.270
she had to learn how to memorize her lines
before she could even read for her role as

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:53.370
Wednesday Addams on The Addams Family television
series.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:57.840
It certainly made no difference, though, since
the show changed her life and made her one

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:01.030
of the most well-known child actors in the
industry.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:05.520
Loring revealed that she didn't have a comprehensive
filmography when she auditioned for Wednesday,

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:09.440
yet she still secured the role over another
young actor auditioning for the part.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:14.300
It seemed surprising that Loring came out
on top since there's often a natural reluctance

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.060
from productions to cast very young children.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:21.500
Loring claimed the reason for her casting
success was because of her uncanny resemblance

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:25.288
to Carolyn Jones, who portrayed her onscreen
mother Morticia.

00:08:25.566 --> 00:08:30.509
Despite The Addams Family television series
finding its audience and becoming a runaway

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:33.520
success, it only lasted for two years on the
air.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:37.779
In an interview with the Television Academy
Foundation, John Astin revealed how surprised

00:08:37.779 --> 00:08:42.120
he was to hear that the show had been canceled,
though he knew the then-president of the network

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:46.190
had a slightly different sense of humor which
may have impacted the abrupt decision.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:51.460
However, Astin expressed how another show's
debut may have also played a pivotal part

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:52.460
in the cancellation.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.209
Astin told the Television Academy Foundation:

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.755
"You shallow brained simpletons, where's your
imagination?

00:09:14.755 --> 00:09:15.755
Your ambition!?"

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:20.779
Astin appeared in Batman, portraying The Riddler
in Season 2 of the show, while Ted Cassidy's

00:09:20.779 --> 00:09:23.089
Lurch also made a guest appearance in an episode.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:28.400
There's sage advice that says never mess with
a winning formula.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:33.209
But in the world of TV executives, they love
nothing more than to tweak and change things,

00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:36.920
even when the show is a smash hit and everything
works well.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:41.279
It turns out The Addams Family television
series wasn't immune to this phenomenon either,

00:09:41.279 --> 00:09:43.562
as John Astin revealed to The A.V. Club.

00:09:43.562 --> 00:09:48.730
The actor gushed about working with producer
and series creator David Levy and head writer

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:53.230
Nat Perrin, explaining how there was a natural
artistic synergy between all parties and how

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.570
it developed into a friendly working relationship.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:00.120
However, the production company decided it
wanted to replace Levy and Perrin, so Astin

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.800
and Caroyln Jones intervened to get their
old crew back.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.870
Astin told The A.V. Club:

00:10:20.862 --> 00:10:25.750
While reboots are fairly common in both film
and television, The Addams Family television

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:30.350
series' unprecedented success scared off potential
suitors from trying to redo it.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:34.900
The franchise lived on through various animated
shows and live-action films, but there was

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.220
a fear of reviving the series until 1998.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:43.120
The New Addams Family featured a brand new
cast, with John Astin later making guest appearances

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.350
as Grandpapa Addams.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:50.430
The show won a few Leo Awards in 2000 and
introduced a new generation to this kooky

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:55.000
family, but it didn't have the same lasting
impact or cultural influence as the original series.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:00.370
Ironically, there's also a misconception that
The New Addams Family was short-lived in comparison

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:01.370
to the original.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:06.430
That's inaccurate, though, since the classic
television series ran for 64 episodes from

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:14.100
1964 to 1966, while The New Addams Family
aired 65 episodes from 1998 to 1999.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:19.220
Of course, the original series returned for
a reunion TV film and the cast provided their

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.290
voices for the characters in other projects.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:26.760
However, The New Addams Family still holds
the distinct honor of lasting for one more

00:11:27.498 --> 00:11:28.668
episode than its predecessor.

